 "title": "Sch9 and TORC1 Regulate pH Homeostasis and Cell Viability",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around the genes and proteins Sch9 and TORC1, which play crucial roles in regulating pH homeostasis and cell viability. Sch9 and TORC1 interact with and regulate various other genes and proteins, including V-ATPase, PKA, and Pma1, to maintain pH balance and ensure cell survival. Additionally, the cluster involves the mitochondria, vacuole, and plasma membrane, which are all affected by the regulatory activities of Sch9 and TORC1. The cluster also touches on the process of longevity, which is involved in V-ATPase, and the chemicals rapamycin and H2O2, which are affected by the regulatory activities of Sch9 and TORC1.",
